        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "A successful response does not end when the microbe disappears. Resolution is active. Alarm signals decline, short-lived cells are cleared, macrophages shift toward repair, and tissue structure is restored. If recognition is weak, infection can spread. If recruitment is excessive or resolution fails, inflammation can persist and injure the host. The complete systems view is therefore barrier, recognition, signaling, recruitment, clearance, and resolution. Each stage supplies a checkpoint for understanding disease and therapeutic intervention."
        },
