        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "Neutrophils and monocytes follow a coordinated recruitment sequence. They slow and roll along activated endothelium, adhere firmly, move between vessel cells, and follow chemical gradients toward the source. At the site, phagocytes engulf microbes and debris, while complement and other soluble factors support recognition and clearance. The visualization makes a key point: immune defense is a movement-and-information problem. Cells must arrive at the right place, in the right state, and in sufficient numbers."
        },
